# Must-fail mutant for legacy-invoices.cache-key.int.test.ts's AC-17
# specification. Paired describes: "legacy-invoices cache — the collection is
# keyed per client (AC-17)" and "legacy-invoices cache — the single read is
# keyed per client (AC-17)".
#
# Mutates `loadList` and `loadOne` in `legacy-invoices.services.ts` — drops the
# `{ client: clientId.value }` segment from BOTH cache keys (design.md §5.1,
# §8.1, §10.1 row 7). Without the client segment, a second client in the same
# tab reads the first client's one-day-stale cache entry instead of a fresh
# per-client request.
#
# Reds (exactly two):
#   - "@AC-17 a second client's archive read issues a fresh request and
#     publishes that client's rows, never the first client's cached rows"
#   - "@AC-17 a second client reading the SAME record id issues a fresh request
#     and publishes that client's record, never the first client's cached
#     record"
#
# Declared collateral: NONE (verified — the full headless integration suite
# stays green with this patch applied, aside from the two named assertions:
# 7 files / 53 tests, of which only the two @AC-17 tests red).
#
# Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.
--- a/packages/headless/src/modules/legacy-invoices/legacy-invoices.services.ts
+++ b/packages/headless/src/modules/legacy-invoices/legacy-invoices.services.ts
